# Build context filter for backend/Dockerfile.
#
# Added with the release CI (.github/workflows). backend/Dockerfile COPYs
# selectively (pyproject.toml, uv.lock, app/, alembic.ini, alembic/), so this
# file is defence in depth rather than a bug fix - but it matters for two
# reasons:
#
# 1. A developer's local state lives in this directory: .venv/ (hundreds of
#    MB), lazyaf.db (their actual cards, repos and history), build/ and
#    *.egg-info/. All of it was being uploaded to the daemon on every build,
#    and any of it becoming COPY'd later would put private data in a PUBLIC
#    image.
#
# 2. A stray `.env` in here must never reach a published image.
#    .github/scripts/scan_image_secrets.py fails the build if one does; this
#    stops it getting that far.
#
# What the image build needs is NOT excluded: pyproject.toml, uv.lock, app/,
# alembic.ini and alembic/ (migrations ship in the image so a fresh volume
# boots to head).

# Local virtualenv and packaging residue.
.venv
build
*.egg-info
.python-version

# Developer database and git-server storage - this is real user data.
*.db
*.sqlite
data
git_repos

# Python bytecode and tool caches.
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Credentials. Never in a build context, never in a published image.
.env
.env.*

# Docker's own files and local noise.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.log
.DS_Store
